WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.760
And then gods took him away.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.410
It must have been cattle mutilation.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:18.760
My grandpa went to sleep at
night and never woke up again.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.250
The cause of his death was unknown.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.060
Gods are evil.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.150
They don't just take intestines when they come for you.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.530
Grandpa's body was beautiful.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.030
Gods are aliens?

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.340
Yes. Gods are aliens.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.040
That's why a lot of things are beyond your control.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.290
The soreness struck me after two days.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.710
Today is Meme-chin's birthday.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.420
No time for laundry or cleaning!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.480
This is the only natural way to relieve my muscle pain.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.570
Who would've thought I would learn from my own daughter — I must have...

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.940
<i>not</i> aged!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.910
I turned into an adult who only thinks and thinks about problems,

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.370
without ever resolving any.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.540
Forty already?

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.290
Heroin! Cocaine!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.710
The next morning, my brother called me,

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.030
so I also asked them how to befriend animals.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.260
Open your mind, you know?

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:41.490
Here you go!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.510
Have a nice day.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.760
Thanks.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.180
Erio told me she wanted to work.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.690
Makoto can keep her company for now.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.980
In the meantime, I have to come up with a way to get her a job.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:22.570
Morning!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.740
Good morning, boss.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.780
I haven't seen you for three days.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.660
Yup, I haven't seen you for three days either,

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.620
so somehow it's all fair!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:41.110
You always make me wonder why you don't ever get depressed with logic like that.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.660
It was a huge praise.
Was that a praise?

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.320
Oh, is this your newest creation?

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.750
You look pretty tired for someone who doesn't work.
Are you all right?

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.410
I'm totally fine. I'm still not gonna work, though.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.800
Marvelous!

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.960
Well then, I'll get going.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.670
Come back before it's time for snack!

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.410
I'll be serious and start working next month.
You can count on me!

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.710
I was just about to get up.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.140
What do you want today?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.430
I came to see you.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.810
You always say that.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.430
I'll do your laundry.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:40.820
Idiot!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:44.690
Didn't I teach you that if you have the time to help me, you should be working instead?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.320
Would you rather take a bath?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.910
I'll take one later.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.120
For now...

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.410
Come on, talk!

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:57.210
I'm not feeling very talkative today.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:05.840
It seems animals are disappearing all over the city lately.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.800
I heard about it last week.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.680
Apparently, it's still going on!

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.020
Cattle mutilation, huh?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.480
Does that excite you?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.730
Does what?

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.440
The aliens!

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.520
They may be somewhere in this town.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.940
You couldn't see them even if they were!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.950
There must be one by my side, even now.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:33.830
Maybe I can wipe them out by going on a rampage in this room!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.330
It's my turn soon.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.050
Granny, what did you think about when you turned forty?

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:51.970
Forty?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:57.220
Oh, right! It was your birthday last week.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:57.680
What?

00:06:58.640 --> 00:06:59.270
Yes...

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.770
I'll give you a present, a snack on the house.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:05.900
That brings back memories.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:13.120
I can usually walk, I just happen to be having a bad day.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.660
Right, I know.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:22.960
She's so light that my sore muscles don't hurt at all when I carry her.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.760
Tired already?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.720
Granny...

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.100
Don't tell me to get down.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.020
I'll wipe them out.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.860
Your bad habit of laziness?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.360
No, I like that habit!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:52.570
Hey, I want to send you a talented worker.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.610
Would you let Erio work here?

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:58.450
I don't think it's a bad idea.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.710
Yay! It's complete!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.040
Whoosh, whoosh!

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.130
The "June 12th" is completed,

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.670
and it's finally time for the test flight.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.720
I already have an idea of a person who can help me, and where I can find him.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.630
Someone's been launching rockets around here recently.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.900
Excuse me!

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.820
Nice to meet you, I'm...

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.610
"Nice to meet you?"

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.030
Huh?

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.370
Meme, I mean...

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.910
You're Touwa, right?

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.330
I used to live here before high school.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.330
Could it be... Yamamoto-kun?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.880
Not even a single character of my name right, including "kun".

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.960
But I pretty much remember who you are now.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.680
But not my name?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.550
When did you return?

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.180
I came back after quitting my job last month.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.190
By the way, I'm single.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:05.520
So what?

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.440
What are you doing here?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.940
Oh, right!

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:16.530
I wanted you to help me with the launch.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:18.990
Here.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.830
Oh, sure.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.380
It's ready.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.130
3, 2, 1, liftoff!

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.470
It's faster than a salamander!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.220
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.310
H-Hey...

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.270
Touwa!

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.860
Why are you launching a rocket, Touwa?

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.820
Don't tell me, you came to see me...

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.830
Or just a hobby?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.790
Preparing to wipe them out.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.790
Huh? Wipe what out?

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.580
Aliens!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.040
With a plastic bottle?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:12.750
Yeah!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.170
I'll bring more to launch, okay?

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.930
Oh, sure...

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.640
Also, I have another request.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.350
Oh? What is it?

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:25.310
I'll do almost anything for you!

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.140
You can count on me!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:33.940
What?

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.110
Pretty please?

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.110
Well, I don't mind, but—

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.360
Yay! Thanks!

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.990
By the way... where's Elliott?

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:49.000
He's not in this city. He went somewhere.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.130
Oh well, later!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.050
Touwa!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:00.050
I mean, Meme-chan.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.260
Well...

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:04.970
Yes?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:09.560
Well, I mean, with me...

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.100
I should get to the point.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.110
What's the matter, Yamamoto?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.440
I told you, I'm not Yamamoto!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.480
Then tell me your na—

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.530
What I'm saying is, marry me!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.070
June 12th,

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:26.120
A gentleman whose name I didn't even know proposed to me.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.540
Wh-What?

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.000
I haven't seen you around before.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.290
What do your parents do?

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.250
Mine run a flower shop.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.090
Mine are in pyrotechnics.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.420
You know, they make fireworks.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.590
Did you see their fireworks in last year's festival?

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.640
Elliott was a foreigner in the same grade.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:51.480
At first, I thought he was one of the aliens that my grandma and grandpa often spoke of.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.900
He was my first love.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.320
Maybe it's almost my turn.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.320
For what?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.860
Cattle mutilation.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.490
What?

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.080
No!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:11.790
God can't be seen, so it's unavoidable.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:18.210
Then I'm going to do something about that whatchamacallit.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.340
How exactly would you do that?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.180
No idea...

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.550
You're giving up already?

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.930
But I don't want Granny to be gone!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.470
I don't...

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:32.850
Okay, okay.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.100
Thank you.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.980
You'd better think hard if you want to save me.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.610
Even a fool will eventually come up with something.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.360
Why don't you just wipe them out?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.330
Why don't you just wipe them out?

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.540
I ran home after he proposed to me.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.790
Before I realized it, I was relaxing in the tub.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.110
Please marry me!

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:09.210
Seriously?

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:14.010
Sheesh, should I turn him down?

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.420
I mean, do I even want to get married?

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.130
With whom?

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.680
I've been living with Erio all this time,

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:24.510
so I'm not confident I can make space for someone else in this house.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.150
Mako-kun is like my own child.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:30.970
I'm really reluctant to accept someone who's unrelated as a family member.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:34.980
I have to come up with something.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:45.340
I probably should've taught Erio how to think of a solution back when she was wrapping herself in futons.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.740
Then she might've stayed in school.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:53.630
My life is filled with regrets,
and I can never be truly satisfied.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.940
For the following week,

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:08.280
I secretly cared for animals so
I wouldn't run into Yamamoto-kun,

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.080
and went to see Erio at work at the Tamura shop.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:22.710
That's where I met a baby-skinned girl,

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.710
and successfully got rid of my cola.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:29.300
Getting hold of empty plastic bottles is actually the hardest part of making rockets.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.510
He's probably looking for me.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.520
Well, if you'll excuse me!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.270
See you!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.890
Why don't you just wipe them out?

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.730
Wipe them out? How?

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.030
The only way to reach something you can't see is faith.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.110
Faith?

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:47.990
Yes.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:52.490
And to demonstrate your faith, you need...

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:54.450
... ceremony and prayer.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.790
So that I can look up to the sky with a smile.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.260
Hey! Shuugorou!

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.800
It's <i>that</i> Yamamoto now?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.100
Stay away from the Yamamoto already!

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.350
Oh?

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:17.430
Don't stay away physically!

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:19.180
You can call me Yamamoto!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.480
So don't run from me!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.570
Uh, are you here to launch the rockets?

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.820
Yes, and also to turn you down.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.910
Wait, I got carried away...

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.990
so I'm sorry!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.580
I'm not offended or anything,

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.950
but I still have to turn you down!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:43.170
Before you do that, at least let me explain!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.080
You bet,

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:45.340
but I still have to turn you down.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.850
I've liked you ever since I was little.

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.850
Well, that's all there is to it.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.350
I quit my job and came back to this city.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.980
That's when I saw you riding your bike,

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.940
full of joy, just like when you were little.

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:15.120
It's like you stole my attention and my heart all over again.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.950
You don't intend to ever get married?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.580
Nope, not at all!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.920
That's a waste.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.000
You're so beautiful.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:32.630
My daughter and nephew are living with me right now,

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.640
and that's more than enough to make me happy.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:37.470
I don't need a husband in my family.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:41.890
I never married Elliott either.
I'm planning to stay single forever.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.060
I see.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:47.310
Okay, then.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.150
Let's start by becoming friends!

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:53.900
Oh? I thought we were already friends?

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.660
You're right.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:03.120
I launched plastic bottle rockets to show them to your daughter.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.790
Really?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.790
But why?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.840
Because I heard she's interested in space.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.210
Oh! You were scheming to get close to me?

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:12.170
Yeah.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.260
That cow tag, too?

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.390
I thought she might like occult subjects like cattle mutilation.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.850
It didn't seem to work, though.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.430
Your daughter is really tall, huh?

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.020
Huh?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:25.230
She must be over 180cm.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.520
How can he possibly get "180cm" from Erio?

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.940
Her three sizes? Wavelength?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:37.280
Who is he talking about? A girl over 180cm tall?

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.030
Yamamoto-kun...

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.660
Right, that's my nickname.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.450
What is it?

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.660
That's not my daughter.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:50.710
What? Isn't she the girl who works at the Japanese sweets shop?

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.710
That's my employee!

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:55.130
But I heard rumors!

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.430
She's the girl who walks around in a strange getup.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:00.890
She did until April, but...

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:01.930
Until April?

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.730
You came back in May, right?

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:07.190
Then you missed seeing Futon Erio in action.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.650
Too bad.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.230
Geez!

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:15.940
I even paid her for a side job to get to know her.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.160
I asked her to make plastic bottle rockets.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.160
What am I going to do with so many of them?

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.330
Lots of rockets? Perfect!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.040
The ceremony will be a magnificent spectacle!

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:31.340
Yamamoto-kun!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.090
Right, that's my name!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.170
Are you ready with that request of mine?

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:41.050
Yeah, it was your request, so I put everything I had into it.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.220
Thank you.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:49.060
You really are the best domino I could lean on.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:56.900
I'm home.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.070
Welcome home!

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:05.830
That evening, I asked Maekawa-chan to get those two to make plastic bottle rockets.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.750
Okay, bye!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.000
What are we going to do with the rockets?

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.500
Launch them, of course!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:20.590
With our prayer, into the distant universe of our dreams.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.480
You can stay in bed, Granny.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.360
Shut up! I want to sit!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.620
Why are you here at this hour?

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.290
Granny, why don't we go to the beach tomorrow?

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:54.130
Huh? You think I can go to the beach at my age?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.500
Are you feeling sick?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:58.760
Idiot! My figure isn't what it used to be!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:01.280
Don't act like your were sexy before, old lady.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:05.660
Don't get carried away just because you have smoother fat than me!

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.520
I'm going to be taken away from this world anyway.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.760
There's no point in doing anything.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.970
That attitude is why,

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:21.600
for the past 28 years...

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.860
Just for one day!

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:26.610
Please!

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:29.230
I haven't seen that in years!

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:34.910
Isn't that what Shouji always said when he asked girls out?

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:37.450
"Just for one day, just one day!"

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.620
Right, he did!

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:43.210
I'm surprised you remembered.

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:47.340
Of course! You told me about it.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:50.050
That he always seemed to be praying.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:54.430
I don't know what's going on, but I'll go!

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:56.800
Thanks.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:20:59.560
I'll get going.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:02.090
Meme.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:08.830
Be safe on your way back. You're a mother now.

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:12.140
Thanks.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.330
See you tomorrow, then!

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.090
You just wait, aliens!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.520
It's hot! My nose is going to dry out!

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:36.020
What's that toy?

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:40.270
All right, Yamamoto-kun!

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.530
Catch this!

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.740
Did you catch it?

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.410
Barely! Warn me next time!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.780
I've heard that voice before.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.160
You have?

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.290
Are you ready?

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.290
Not yet!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.710
That voice too.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:00.040
You're well connected, eh, Granny?

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.460
Are you ready?

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:04.460
I don't think so!

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.340
Shouji's son?

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:08.590
Are you ready?

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:10.100
Not yet!

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.850
I don't know her.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:15.680
I just added a new character to your network!

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:18.690
Are you ready?

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:21.110
I'm ready...

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:23.820
So unmotivated.

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:26.900
Are you ready?

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:29.660
We're ready!

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.620
Okay, let's do it!

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:43.000
We're not done just yet!

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:50.050
Who made that one? Ms. Clumsy?

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:53.890
Granny, are you watching?

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:56.270
Is this...

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:57.060
There's the next one!

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:03.980
Look, look! The "June 17th" is flying so well!

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:06.480
Look at it go!

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:09.150
Wait!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:13.910
It's gone...

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:19.620
Elliott, you idiot!

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:22.960
The ceremony ain't over till the fat lady sings!

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:29.970
Just a little more... a little more... a little more!

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:32.300
Reach them, reach them, reach them!

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:35.560
Hit the aliens! Hit the bullseye!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.930
Yamamoto-ya!

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:42.150
Go!

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:53.780
Elliott, I gave it a try.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:57.080
I tried my best. Did I wipe them out?

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:01.830
You... was that...

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:04.670
Do you feel alive, for the first time in ages?

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:09.170
Aliens and despair within Granny, are you all wiped out?

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:16.510
It was refreshing enough for me to recall a bunch of stupid memories.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.890
We fooled the aliens with decoys,

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.770
and finished them off with the big one!

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:25.150
The hand-made rocket by Yamamoto-kun, son of the firework maker.

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:28.190
So, that voice earlier was Ashiro's.

00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:30.570
Oh, was that his name?

00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:33.030
Is that all?

00:24:33.030 --> 00:24:34.570
Yup, that's all.

00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:37.370
This is what you've been thinking about?

00:24:37.370 --> 00:24:38.370
It is.

00:24:38.370 --> 00:24:39.580
The whole time?

00:24:39.580 --> 00:24:41.120
The <i>whole</i> time.

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:44.670
Anyway, I wiped them out.

00:24:44.670 --> 00:24:48.170
That's why God won't take you anytime soon.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:53.590
What do <i>you</i> know about aliens?

00:24:57.310 --> 00:25:01.920
His potential is ridiculously high for a son of Shouji's.

00:25:02.900 --> 00:25:05.620
What was your first impression of Mako-kun?

00:25:05.620 --> 00:25:10.760
When he came over with Erio for the first time, I thought it was Shouji who came with you.

00:25:10.760 --> 00:25:12.690
I thought my life was flashing before my eyes!

00:25:13.020 --> 00:25:14.980
You're such a pessimistic grandma.

00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:17.970
I've been like this ever since Grandpa passed away.

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:20.900
I had such a low expectations for everything

00:25:20.900 --> 00:25:24.460
because I didn't have enough energy to regret my actions when things went wrong.

00:25:24.960 --> 00:25:31.730
I just kept on hating the gods and accepted the unfairness of life.

00:25:32.180 --> 00:25:34.550
They're an invisible enemy, after all.

00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:37.930
There's no way to relieve my stress and hatred.

00:25:37.930 --> 00:25:41.240
That's how I coped with this whole "fate" thing.

00:25:41.240 --> 00:25:47.230
It made me pessimistic, and it was painful, but I can accept it and live on.

00:25:47.230 --> 00:25:50.730
Even if my husband and daughter died,

00:25:50.730 --> 00:25:56.730
even if I was the only one who lived long enough to see my great-grandchild. Yet...

00:25:59.450 --> 00:26:00.290
I'm sorry.

00:26:00.290 --> 00:26:02.490
It's nothing for you to apologize about.

00:26:02.920 --> 00:26:06.120
Idiots just do unexpected things.

00:26:07.590 --> 00:26:11.090
Are you the one who taught her about being wrapped in futon?

00:26:11.090 --> 00:26:13.410
No. She came up with it on her own.

00:26:16.490 --> 00:26:18.870
That was Grandpa's old habit.

00:26:18.870 --> 00:26:22.570
He always ran into a futon whenever he was under pressure.

00:26:22.570 --> 00:26:24.860
It runs in the blood, huh?

00:26:24.860 --> 00:26:26.760
Isn't it weird sometimes?

00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:31.670
We're bound by things like blood and fate.
We're all linked like dominoes,

00:26:32.390 --> 00:26:35.150
and it's impossible to resist it,

00:26:35.150 --> 00:26:40.930
but sometimes I think we can at least change the direction the dominoes fall.

00:26:42.430 --> 00:26:45.640
I'll leave the shop to Erio when I die.

00:26:45.640 --> 00:26:46.680
Geez!

00:26:46.680 --> 00:26:48.930
I'm not going anywhere just yet, though!

00:26:50.980 --> 00:26:52.350
Hey, Granny!

00:26:54.190 --> 00:26:56.940
Would you mind if we took a detour on the way back?

00:26:58.690 --> 00:27:02.800
Sure! The shop's closed for today.

00:27:07.410 --> 00:27:11.940
Like there's anything better than hanging out with my granddaughter!

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:16.380
I'll go visit Grampa's grave with Granny.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:20.050
I've already decided what I'll tell him first.

00:27:20.630 --> 00:27:26.260
I'm going to tell him that we're still living our lives, even after parting with so many people.

00:27:27.010 --> 00:27:29.310
I've turned forty.

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:03.440
Muscle pain ouchy!: -1

00:29:03.440 --> 00:29:04.900
Deciding to work: +3

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:06.950
Granny is pessimistic: -2

00:29:06.950 --> 00:29:09.320
I will be working at the Tamura shop: +2

00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:11.120
He proposed to me: -1

00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:14.080
Birthday celebration at the beach: +3 for my cousin and me.

00:29:14.080 --> 00:29:16.160
Turned forty happily: +5

00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:19.080
Current return-to-society points total: +8

00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:21.670
Current happiness points total: +1

00:29:21.670 --> 00:29:24.380
Next time: A Local Alien Sighting.

00:29:24.380 --> 00:29:26.380
Erio, aren't you forgetting something?

00:29:26.380 --> 00:29:30.240
The cousin's current adolescence points total: +2
